### **SECTION 1: WHAT IS CYBER ESSENTIALS? (IASME Website)**

**Full Text:**

```
Cyber Essentials is the UK Government's minimum baseline standard for 
cyber security for organisations of all sizes. The annually renewable 
certification scheme is aligned to five technical controls designed to 
prevent the most common internet-based cyber security threats.

Cyber Essentials certification includes automatic cyber liability insurance 
for any UK organisation who certifies their whole organisation and has 
less than £20m annual turnover.

All the assessment questions are available to download for free in 
advance. Once you have passed Cyber Essentials, you can progress to 
Cyber Essentials Plus, which is a hands-on audit of your systems.
```

**Key Points:**
- UK Government minimum baseline standard
- Annually renewable (12-month validity)
- Five technical controls
- Free insurance included (conditions apply)
- Questions available in advance
- Two levels: CE and CE Plus

