### **SECTION 3: CERTIFICATION PROCESS (Assessment Journey)**

**Full Text:**

```
I'm ready to certify for Cyber Essentials

When you are ready, you will need to register for certification and make 
a payment. Once your application and payment have been received, you 
will receive your online assessment portal log-in details so that you can 
enter your answers into the on-line assessment platform. A senior member 
of the board or equivalent from your organisation must e-sign a document 
to verify that all the answers are true and then a qualified external 
Assessor will mark the answers.

Once you have submitted your assessment for marking, your Assessor may 
send you feedback. You then have 2 working days to address any feedback 
and resubmit. Once you pass, you will receive your certificate and be 
listed on our directory of certified organisations.

You will need to renew your certificate annually as it expires after 
twelve months. We remove companies from our certified organisation list 
if they are not re-certified within twelve months of their last 
certificate.
```

**Process Flow:**

```
Step 1: PURCHASE
→ Register online
→ Make payment
→ Receive portal login (via email)

Step 2: COMPLETE ASSESSMENT
→ Log into online platform
→ Answer all questions
→ Board member e-signs declaration

Step 3: SUBMIT FOR MARKING
→ Independent Assessor reviews
→ Feedback provided (if needed)
→ 2 working days to address feedback

Step 4: PASS & CERTIFICATION
→ Receive certificate (PDF)
→ Listed in public directory
→ Display badge on website/email

Step 5: RENEWAL (Annual)
→ Certificate expires after 12 months
→ Must re-certify to remain listed
→ Removal if not renewed within 12 months
```

**Timeline:**
- Application to login: 1-2 business days
- Complete assessment: Varies (typically 1-4 weeks for SMEs)
- Assessor marking: 2-5 business days
- Feedback response: 2 working days deadline
- Certificate issuance: 1-2 business days after pass

